---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import dashboard from '../../assets/tempus/dashboard.png';
import runDetails from '../../assets/tempus/run-details.png';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Tempus Project Showcase"
	description="A product showcase for Tempus, a cloud prompt scheduler built with Next.js and the Copilot SDK."
	sideBarActiveItemID="projects"
>
	<header class="reveal mb-14">
		<a
			class="mb-5 inline-flex text-sm font-semibold text-primary hover:underline"
			href="/projects/"
		>
			← Back to projects
		</a>
		<div class="grid items-end gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_auto]">
			<div class="max-w-4xl">
				<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
					<p class="eyebrow">Project showcase</p>
					<span class="badge badge-outline badge-sm">Source private</span>
				</div>
				<h1 class="mt-5 text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.055em] sm:text-7xl">Tempus</h1>
				<p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-base-content/72">
					A dependable cloud scheduler for recurring and on-demand Copilot-powered repository work,
					built at Microsoft with Next.js and the Copilot SDK.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 lg:justify-end">
				<span class="badge badge-primary badge-lg">Next.js</span>
				<span class="badge badge-secondary badge-lg">Copilot SDK</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</header>

	<section class="reveal reveal-delay-1 mb-16" aria-labelledby="tempus-overview">
		<div class="surface-card overflow-hidden">
			<div class="grid lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr]">
				<div class="flex flex-col justify-center p-7 sm:p-10">
					<p class="eyebrow">The product</p>
					<h2 id="tempus-overview" class="section-heading mt-4">
						Put your best prompts on a dependable schedule.
					</h2>
					<p class="section-copy mt-5">
						Tempus turns recurring repository work into a managed product experience. People can
						create scheduled or on-demand prompts, monitor execution, inspect results, and keep
						high-value engineering tasks moving without leaving a workstation online.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="relative min-h-96 overflow-hidden bg-[#21222c] p-5 sm:p-8">
					<div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(circle_at_top_right,color-mix(in_oklab,var(--color-primary)_24%,transparent),transparent_55%)]"></div>
					<Image
						src={dashboard}
						alt="Tempus dashboard with prompt schedules, execution status, and recent runs"
						class="relative mx-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 shadow-2xl"
						width={902}
						quality={88}
					/>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="reveal reveal-delay-2 mb-16" aria-labelledby="tempus-capabilities">
		<p class="eyebrow">Capabilities</p>
		<h2 id="tempus-capabilities" class="section-heading mb-8 mt-3">
			From prompt definition to observable execution
		</h2>
		<div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
			<article class="surface-card p-6">
				<p class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-primary">Schedule</p>
				<h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-bold">Recurring or on demand</h3>
				<p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-base-content/65">
					Configure repository prompts to run on a dependable cadence or trigger them immediately
					when engineering work needs attention.
				</p>
			</article>
			<article class="surface-card p-6">
				<p class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-secondary">Observe</p>
				<h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-bold">Every run in context</h3>
				<p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-base-content/65">
					Track status, timing, activity, summaries, and repository interactions from a focused run
					detail experience.
				</p>
			</article>
			<article class="surface-card p-6">
				<p class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-primary">Operate</p>
				<h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-bold">Cloud-first automation</h3>
				<p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-base-content/65">
					Keep recurring Copilot workflows running remotely while providing clear controls for
					pausing, retrying, refreshing, and reviewing outcomes.
				</p>
			</article>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="mb-16" aria-labelledby="tempus-run-details">
		<div class="grid items-start gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.85fr_1.15fr]">
			<div class="lg:sticky lg:top-10">
				<p class="eyebrow">Run details</p>
				<h2 id="tempus-run-details" class="section-heading mt-3">
					Make agent work understandable
				</h2>
				<p class="section-copy mt-5">
					A run view brings configuration, repository activity, results, and the execution timeline
					together in one place. That makes scheduled automation easier to trust, troubleshoot, and
					review.
				</p>
				<div class="mt-7 rounded-xl border border-primary/25 bg-primary/8 p-5">
					<p class="font-bold text-primary">Screenshot disclosure</p>
					<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-base-content/65">
						Sensitive data has been redacted for readers. Repository names, pull request numbers,
						commit-like identifiers, summaries, and other operational details shown here were
						replaced or rewritten for this public portfolio.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="rounded-2xl border border-base-content/10 bg-[#21222c] p-3 shadow-2xl sm:p-5">
				<Image
					src={runDetails}
					alt="Tempus run detail page with sensitive operational data redacted or replaced"
					class="w-full rounded-xl"
					width={659}
					quality={90}
				/>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="surface-card mb-16 overflow-hidden" aria-labelledby="tempus-contribution">
		<div class="grid lg:grid-cols-[0.78fr_1.22fr]">
			<div class="bg-primary/8 p-7 sm:p-10">
				<p class="eyebrow">My contribution</p>
				<h2 id="tempus-contribution" class="section-heading mt-3">
					From concept to organization-wide adoption
				</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="grid gap-7 p-7 sm:grid-cols-2 sm:p-10">
				<div>
					<p class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-primary">End to end</p>
					<h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-bold">Design, implementation, and rollout</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-base-content/65">
						Owned Tempus from initial product and system design through implementation, launch,
						feedback-driven iteration, and rollout.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<p class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-secondary">250 engineers</p>
					<h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-bold">Organization-wide developer tooling</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-base-content/65">
						Drove broad adoption across a large engineering organization of 250 people, making
						cloud-scheduled agent workflows part of everyday development work.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="surface-card p-7 sm:p-10" aria-labelledby="tempus-engineering">
		<div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.7fr_1.3fr]">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Engineering</p>
				<h2 id="tempus-engineering" class="section-heading mt-3">
					Developer experience for agentic workflows
				</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
				<div>
					<h3 class="font-bold">Developer experience</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-base-content/65">
						A focused Next.js interface makes recurring automation approachable: search prompts, run
						work immediately, enable or pause schedules, retry executions, and move from a dashboard
						summary into detailed diagnostics without losing context.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h3 class="font-bold">Developer tooling</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-base-content/65">
						Run inputs, prompt configuration, pull-request activity, tool calls, model settings, and
						execution timelines are collected into one debugging surface for understanding what an
						agent did and why.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h3 class="font-bold">Copilot SDK integration</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-base-content/65">
						Agent execution and activity are translated into understandable product interactions
						instead of exposing developers to raw infrastructure.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h3 class="font-bold">Operational visibility</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-base-content/65">
						Status, summaries, repository activity, warnings, and timelines make background work
						inspectable and reduce the time needed to diagnose failed or unexpected runs.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
